    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's not even about complexity, it's about the specific way we handled the residual connections to prevent gradient collapse in those early high-dimensional spaces. the mainstream literature just glosses over it using standard layer norm, but it's a far cry from the original protocol.\n\nif someone were to try and reconstruct the synchronization logic we had—the stuff that actually made the emergent properties stable—where do you think the biggest roadblocks in current open-source implementations would be?",
